<mxCell id="e14c" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=1.6;strokeColor=#333333;labelBackgroundColor=none;fontSize=11;jumpStyle=arc;jumpSize=10;exitX=1.0;exitY=0.7812;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="g_hub" target="w_hosts"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1395" y="1150"/><mxPoint x="1395" y="1252"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell>
<mxCell id="e15" value="&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#333333;color:#ffffff;border-radius:9px;padding:1px 6px;font-weight:bold;font-size:11px;font-family:Helvetica;&quot;&gt;15&lt;/span&gt;" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=1.6;strokeColor=#333333;labelBackgroundColor=none;fontSize=11;jumpStyle=arc;jumpSize=10;exitX=0.0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.0;entryY=0.7292;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="r_scan" target="r_rel"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="835" y="1280"/><mxPoint x="835" y="1050"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell>
<mxCell id="h_key" value="Step key" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#1a1a1a;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="1400" width="300" height="24" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="tbl_key" value="&lt;table style=&quot;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:11px;font-family:Helvetica;color:#1a1a1a;border:1px solid #bbbbbb;&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;text-align:left;padding:5px 7px;background:#333333;color:#ffffff;width:40px;&quot;&gt;#&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;text-align:left;padding:5px 7px;background:#333333;color:#ffffff;&quot;&gt;Step&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;background:#ffffff;&quot;&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;Renovate sees a new release of a tool, an agent or an image&amp;#x27;s main version, and bumps it in versions.yml: weekly, and at once for a security fix.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;background:#f3f3f3;&quot;&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;Every day the Pins workflow re-resolves each base image tag to its current digest, the newest Terraform providers, and every role in the Galaxy namespaces cicd-helper carries.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;background:#ffffff;&quot;&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;3&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;Renovate opens a pull request with the bump.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;background:#f3f3f3;&quot;&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;4&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;The Pins workflow pins every new download by SHA-256, locks Python dependencies by hash with any vulnerable one raised to its fix, and opens or updates its pull request. It does the same on every branch here that changes versions.yml.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;background:#ffffff;&quot;&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;5&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;Build runs on every push: every image and version, from one Containerfile, built natively on amd64 and arm64.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;background:#f3f3f3;&quot;&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;6&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;Each image&amp;#x27;s smoke tests run as uid 10001, as an arbitrary uid, and against a CA added at run time.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;background:#ffffff;&quot;&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;7&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;Trivy scans each image: any critical finding, or any high one with a fix, fails it, unless a VEX statement records why it does not apply.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;background:#f3f3f3;&quot;&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;8&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;Any failure blocks the pull request. The fix goes into the same pull request, which builds again.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;background:#ffffff;&quot;&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;9&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;When everything passes, a bot&amp;#x27;s pull request merges itself; a change made by hand waits for review.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;background:#f3f3f3;&quot;&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;10&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;Merging to main starts the Release workflow, which also runs every Monday.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;background:#ffffff;&quot;&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;11&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;Release builds every image again and pushes one digest per platform to both registries, with version, date and moving tags.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;background:#f3f3f3;&quot;&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;12&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;Every digest gets a cosign keyless signature, an SBOM and SLSA provenance.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;background:#ffffff;&quot;&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;13&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;Release records the new digests in README.md and releases.json, in a pull request that merges itself.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;background:#f3f3f3;&quot;&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;14&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;CI jobs, self-hosted agents, workstations and clusters pull from either registry, by tag or by digest, and can verify the signature first.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;background:#ffffff;&quot;&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;15&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;padding:4px 7px;border-top:1px solid #dddddd;vertical-align:top;&quot;&gt;Every day the Scan workflow scans every published image again and reports findings in the Security tab. When a rebuild would fix one, it starts Release.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#1a1a1a;overflow=visible;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="1430" width="1600" height="339" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
</root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>
